1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,133
Three hundred applications land in the job portal overnight.

2
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:07,099
Your recruiters have two days,

3
00:00:07,099 --> 00:00:10,114
one phone each, and a hiring manager who wants

4
00:00:10,114 --> 00:00:13,129
a shortlist by Friday. Every profile has to be

5
00:00:13,129 --> 00:00:16,340
filtered, downloaded, called, judged and pitched,

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,896
and every one of those steps is done by

7
00:00:18,896 --> 00:00:19,224
hand.

8
00:00:19,974 --> 00:00:22,440
What if an agent filtered the portal,

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:26,107
downloaded the profiles, prepared every screening call,

10
00:00:26,107 --> 00:00:29,373
scored English proficiency, experience, location,

11
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:32,439
salary ask and working hours against the role,

12
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:35,639
and drafted the pitch, while a person made every

13
00:00:35,639 --> 00:00:39,238
decision that matters? That is hiring flow automation,

14
00:00:39,238 --> 00:00:41,238
done with Claude, done safely.

15
00:00:41,988 --> 00:00:46,356
Gennoor Tech presents HR Hiring Flow Automation with Claude.

16
00:00:47,106 --> 00:00:49,652
One job requisition in. One approved,

17
00:00:49,652 --> 00:00:53,642
documented shortlist out. You build the hiring pipeline in

18
00:00:53,642 --> 00:00:55,707
ten modules across three days,

19
00:00:55,707 --> 00:00:58,665
and every module is something you can test,

20
00:00:58,665 --> 00:01:01,211
review and demonstrate. Claude plans,

21
00:01:01,211 --> 00:01:05,064
drafts and explains. Deterministic Python code executes.

22
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:08,642
A recruiter approves every outreach and every pitch.

23
00:01:08,642 --> 00:01:10,362
And everything is logged.

24
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:13,823
You begin by mapping the real hiring flow,

25
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:16,470
from the job portal of your choice to the

26
00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:19,956
onboarding ticket, and by deciding which steps a model

27
00:01:19,956 --> 00:01:23,055
may propose and which only a person may approve.

28
00:01:23,055 --> 00:01:25,767
Then you set up Claude Code with a project

29
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:27,832
file that encodes hiring policy,

30
00:01:27,832 --> 00:01:29,963
the Claude Agent S D K in Python,

31
00:01:29,963 --> 00:01:33,384
and a Model Context Protocol server that exposes your

32
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:36,935
portal exports and candidate store as tools with strict

33
00:01:36,935 --> 00:01:37,968
J S O N outputs.

34
00:01:38,718 --> 00:01:42,657
Next comes sourcing. You filter and download candidate data

35
00:01:42,657 --> 00:01:45,795
from portal exports and sanctioned portal A P I

36
00:01:45,795 --> 00:01:48,733
endpoints, validate every row with Pydantic,

37
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:52,873
deduplicate across portals, and record where every record came

38
00:01:52,873 --> 00:01:56,344
from. A typed candidate profile captures experience,

39
00:01:56,344 --> 00:01:59,616
location, salary ask and preferred working hours,

40
00:01:59,616 --> 00:02:03,021
extracted from resumes with a confidence per field.

41
00:02:03,021 --> 00:02:05,358
Unknowns are marked, never guessed.

42
00:02:06,108 --> 00:02:08,261
On day two you reach the candidate.

43
00:02:08,261 --> 00:02:11,030
Claude drafts a call script from the role and

44
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:14,414
the profile, and a deterministic scheduler books a slot

45
00:02:14,414 --> 00:02:17,736
in the candidate's preferred hours and places the call

46
00:02:17,736 --> 00:02:21,550
through Twilio Programmable Voice, with recorded consent and a

47
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:23,827
transcript stored against the record.

48
00:02:23,827 --> 00:02:25,365
The script is a proposal.

49
00:02:25,365 --> 00:02:27,088
The recruiter runs the call,

50
00:02:27,088 --> 00:02:29,364
and nothing dials until they say yes.

51
00:02:30,114 --> 00:02:34,631
Then assessment. A rubric-driven agent scores English proficiency from

52
00:02:34,631 --> 00:02:37,213
the transcript on C E F R aligned bands,

53
00:02:37,213 --> 00:02:41,407
checks experience, location, working hours and salary ask against

54
00:02:41,407 --> 00:02:44,957
the requisition, and cites the exact lines that justify

55
00:02:44,957 --> 00:02:47,861
each score. Low confidence routes to a human.

56
00:02:47,861 --> 00:02:51,539
A pitch generator then drafts a personalised pitch within

57
00:02:51,539 --> 00:02:54,959
approved talking points and the approved salary band.

58
00:02:54,959 --> 00:02:57,734
Ask it to promise a number outside the band

59
00:02:57,734 --> 00:03:00,638
and it refuses. And nothing is sent until the

60
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:02,058
recruiter approves it.

61
00:03:02,808 --> 00:03:06,569
Day three is control. You build the guardrails specific

62
00:03:06,569 --> 00:03:08,620
to hiring: P I I minimisation,

63
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:13,476
consent and retention tracking, prompt injection defences for untrusted

64
00:03:13,476 --> 00:03:18,057
resume and transcript text, fairness checks on score distributions,

65
00:03:18,057 --> 00:03:20,998
and an append-only audit log in PostgreSQL.

66
00:03:20,998 --> 00:03:25,237
Every shortlist, every outreach and every pitch passes through

67
00:03:25,237 --> 00:03:27,904
an approval gate with a named approver,

68
00:03:27,904 --> 00:03:30,024
and every override is recorded.

69
00:03:30,774 --> 00:03:34,933
Finally orchestration. The pipeline runs as a FastAPI service

70
00:03:34,933 --> 00:03:37,320
with pytest coverage. Every prompt,

71
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,797
rubric and schema change goes through a GitHub pull

72
00:03:40,797 --> 00:03:44,752
request, and GitHub Actions runs the evaluation set before

73
00:03:44,752 --> 00:03:47,207
it merges. When a candidate accepts,

74
00:03:47,207 --> 00:03:50,548
a ServiceNow record is opened through the Table A

75
00:03:50,548 --> 00:03:53,752
P I so onboarding and access requests start the

76
00:03:53,752 --> 00:03:54,366
same day.

77
00:03:55,116 --> 00:03:57,411
Every lab uses synthetic candidates,

78
00:03:57,411 --> 00:04:00,980
synthetic portal exports and a sandbox telephony number.

79
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:04,167
You will watch a resume try to inject instructions

80
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:05,760
into the scorer and fail.

81
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:08,309
You will see the gate block a pitch that

82
00:04:08,309 --> 00:04:11,305
quotes the wrong salary. And you will trace one

83
00:04:11,305 --> 00:04:14,301
candidate from portal row to onboarding ticket,

84
00:04:14,301 --> 00:04:16,404
event by event, in the audit log.

